According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global off highway vehicle telematics market was valued at USD 2.45 billion in 2025 and will grow to USD 4.12 billion by 2034, reflecting a compound annual growth rate of approximately 5.8 % over the forecast horizon.
Off highway vehicle telematics refers to the integration of connectivity modules, GPS positioning, sensor fusion and advanced analytics into machines such as construction equipment, agricultural tractors, mining loaders and forestry harvesters. The technology enables real time monitoring of engine performance, fuel consumption, location tracking and predictive maintenance alerts while also supporting remote diagnostics, geofencing compliance and usage based insurance models. Because operators can anticipate component wear before failure, maintenance shifts from reactive repairs toward condition based scheduling, which lowers overall operating costs and improves fleet productivity.
